  "slug": "polymorphism-telomere-777b",
  "summary": "Reference-quality assemblies and annotation pipelines now enable resistance-gene and resource discovery directly in non-model eukaryotic genomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these items is the construction and annotation of genomic resources for non-model eukaryotes, where reference quality constrains downstream analysis. HRPv2 provides an automated, reproducible method for full-length homology-based NB-LRR resistance gene prediction directly on genome assemblies, presented as an improved successor to HRP. The Tanacetum vulgare study reports a chromosome-scale HiFi and Iso-Seq assembly and annotation of an invasive North American Asteraceae species, providing a new reference genome. The Pinus edulis study builds a multi-tissue reference transcriptome, reports that tissue sampling yields complementary transcripts, and uses it to design an exon-capture probe set for genomic resource development. The items differ in organism, data type, and goal; they share a resource-building emphasis rather than a common method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-12"
}
